        MoodNode(id: "subject", level: 2, parent: "root", title: "One person or two",
                 rule: "When the same person wants, feels or does both things, Spanish usually uses the infinitive: quiero ir. When it's someone else, que + subjunctive: quiero que vayas. The steps show where the infinitive is a must, where both work, and where the rule doesn't apply.",
